From: cfm-edge
Subject: [PATCH] answer as "cfm-edge" in the Server header and error pages

So a curl/scan shows at once that the CFM edge answered, not the origin
(Apache/LiteSpeed behind it). server_tokens keeps its meaning:
  off   -> Server: cfm-edge            (CFM's config sets off)
  on    -> Server: cfm-edge/<nginx version>
  build -> Server: cfm-edge/<nginx version> (<build>)
Same on HTTP/1, HTTP/2 (the off value was a pre-Huffman-coded "nginx"; it is
now encoded once at runtime, like the versioned value already was) and HTTP/3,
and in the default error page footer.

NGINX_VER is NOT changed: `cfm-edge -v` still prints "nginx version:
nginx/X", which CFM's edgeengine.ParseVersionToken reads.

--- a/src/core/nginx.h	2026-11-11 17:48:23.000000000 +0000
+++ b/src/core/nginx.h	2026-11-19 16:31:43.516148755 +0000
@@ -20,6 +20,17 @@
 #endif
 
 #define NGINX_VAR          "NGINX"
+
+/* cfm-edge: the name this edge answers with (Server header, error page
+ * footer) on HTTP/1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3. NGINX_VER is left alone: `-v` keeps
+ * printing "nginx version: nginx/X", which is what tools parse. */
+#define NGX_EDGE_NAME      "cfm-edge"
+#define NGX_EDGE_VER       NGX_EDGE_NAME "/" NGINX_VERSION
+#ifdef NGX_BUILD
+#define NGX_EDGE_VER_BUILD NGX_EDGE_VER " (" NGX_BUILD ")"
+#else
+#define NGX_EDGE_VER_BUILD NGX_EDGE_VER
+#endif
 #define NGX_OLDPID_EXT     ".oldbin"
 
 
